    <title>A Small Model That Cites Its
  Sources</title>
    <summary>  We show that requiring a model to quote the source sentence removes
most fabricated fields. On a set of 400 documents the error rate falls from
18 percent to under 2 percent.
</summary>
    <author><name>Ada Rivers</name></author>
